{title: It Is Well With My Soul}
{artist: Horatio G. Spafford, 1873; music Philip P. Bliss, 1876}
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 72}
{copyright: Words and music: public domain. Chords © 2026 Simon Davy.}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]When peace like a [G]river at[D]tendeth my way,
When [D]sorrows like [A]sea billows [D]roll;
What[D]ever my lot, Thou hast [G]taught me to [D]say,
[D]It is well, it is [A]well with my [D]soul.

{comment: Chorus}
[D]It is well (it is well), with my [G]soul (with my soul),
[D]It is well, it is [A]well with my [D]soul.

{comment: Verse 2}
Though [D]Satan should [G]buffet, though [D]trials should come,
Let [D]this blest as[A]surance con[D]trol,
That [D]Christ hath re[G]garded my [D]helpless estate,
And [D]hath shed His own [A]blood for my [D]soul.

{comment: Verse 3}
My [D]sin, oh, the [G]bliss of this [D]glorious thought,
My [D]sin, not in [A]part but the [D]whole,
Is [D]nailed to the [G]cross, and I [D]bear it no more,
[D]Praise the Lord, [A]praise the Lord, O my [D]soul!

{comment: Verse 4}
And, [D]Lord, haste the [G]day when the [D]faith shall be sight,
The [D]clouds be rolled [A]back as a [D]scroll;
The [D]trump shall re[G]sound, and the [D]Lord shall de[A]scend,
Even [D]so, it is [A]well with my [D]soul.
